{
  "$comment": [
    "The subject catalogue, migrated from legacy db/db_data/subject_config.json.",
    "",
    "A catalogue row says the subject EXISTS. It does not claim any content has",
    "been written for it — that is a textbook, and textbooks are imported.",
    "",
    "This matters because a textbook cannot be created for a subject that is",
    "absent: the authoring service resolves the coordinate and refuses with",
    "content.coordinate_not_found. Seeding only MATH is why the converted",
    "national science curriculum failed to import on its first attempt.",
    "",
    "Legacy carried 13 subjects. SOCIAL is renamed CIV here to match the",
    "converted curriculum packages, which use CIV for التربية الوطنية.",
    "",
    "The section is named after the Prisma model (Subject) and every field is",
    "a real column on it.",
    "",
    "standardGradeLevels is the legacy provisioningPolicy.gradeLevels, verbatim:",
    "which grade ORDINALS the national curriculum offers the subject in.",
    "SOCIAL→CIV carries SOCIAL's policy; ART has no legacy counterpart and",
    "therefore no standard policy — its distribution is the administrator's",
    "call. Seeded into Subject.standardGradeLevels and expanded once into",
    "grade_subjects; the fill action reads the column, never this file."
  ],
